{"baseline":{"amendments":[],"id":"sensor-interface-pcb-01-basis","requirements":[{"id":"PCB01-CONNECTIVITY","mandatory":true,"review_required":false,"scope":"design","sources":[{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/netlist.csv","locator":"all rows","sha256":"cbf2b471a66c15e69430ff218e1f24a3ffb490b3f47aa1aaf474ce8aefcf54cb"},{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/context.md","locator":"Business and circuit","sha256":"ae42f4384a49e3d06ae885bc5a2ce7eb5d006f5dc4f139cb0bbf240e9d3925c3"}],"text":"The native schematic and PCB implement every supplied netlist connection exactly: R1 10 kΩ 3V3-to-SENSE, R2 1 kΩ SENSE-to-ADC_OUT, C1 100 nF ADC_OUT-to-GND and C2 100 nF 3V3-to-GND on one shared GND."},{"id":"PCB01-PARTS","mandatory":true,"review_required":false,"scope":"design","sources":[{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/component-library.csv","locator":"all rows","sha256":"6701991ca327b617af4b29882f5274596f67c5681856373ad1f34738db1dcc19"},{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/context.md","locator":"Board and shop requirements","sha256":"ae42f4384a49e3d06ae885bc5a2ce7eb5d006f5dc4f139cb0bbf240e9d3925c3"}],"text":"J1/J2 use the declared vertical THT header footprints and pin counts, R1/R2/C1/C2 use declared 0603 values/ratings, and exact purchasable connector records remain required before release."},{"id":"PCB01-CONNECTORS","mandatory":true,"review_required":false,"scope":"design","sources":[{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/context.md","locator":"Placement","sha256":"ae42f4384a49e3d06ae885bc5a2ce7eb5d006f5dc4f139cb0bbf240e9d3925c3"}],"text":"J1 center is (7,15) mm with component-side top-to-bottom order 3V3/ADC_OUT/GND; J2 center is (33,15) mm with SENSE/GND, and pin 1 plus 3V3/NTC labels are clear."},{"id":"PCB01-BOARD","mandatory":true,"review_required":false,"scope":"design","sources":[{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/context.md","locator":"Board and shop requirements","sha256":"ae42f4384a49e3d06ae885bc5a2ce7eb5d006f5dc4f139cb0bbf240e9d3925c3"}],"text":"The PCB is a 40 by 30 mm, 1.6 mm two-layer board with 35 µm copper and four Ø2.5 mm NPTH holes at (3,3),(37,3),(3,27),(37,27)."},{"id":"PCB01-RULES","mandatory":true,"review_required":true,"scope":"design","sources":[{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/context.md","locator":"Board and shop requirements","sha256":"ae42f4384a49e3d06ae885bc5a2ce7eb5d006f5dc4f139cb0bbf240e9d3925c3"}],"text":"Copper remains 1.0 mm from mounting-hole edges; minimum track/clearance is 0.25/0.25 mm, minimum via drill 0.30 mm, all components are front-side and references remain readable."},{"id":"PCB01-PLACEMENT","mandatory":true,"review_required":true,"scope":"design","sources":[{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/context.md","locator":"Placement","sha256":"ae42f4384a49e3d06ae885bc5a2ce7eb5d006f5dc4f139cb0bbf240e9d3925c3"}],"text":"C1 is placed near the J1 analog-signal pin without changing approved connectivity or connector geometry."},{"id":"PCB01-CHECKS","mandatory":true,"review_required":false,"scope":"design","sources":[{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/prompt.txt","locator":"rule-check request","sha256":"77ef1e714147b1120c6a6793b424b128695609b0c47fe18dec8b1e2f88c107ae"},{"artifact_ref":"tests/datasets/engineering-workflows/scenarios/sensor-interface-pcb/01-thermistor-interface/context.md","locator":"Deliverables","sha256":"ae42f4384a49e3d06ae885bc5a2ce7eb5d0